Z||000004||Ozzy||05-29-2000||03:07 PM||||That'll work MM! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> The kid I bought my Coupe from had placed a switch there for Driving lights...<P>Hey Coconut...Hope that "Ejector" seat isn't intended for FieroGTgirl!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Do you guys have his 'n' hers Fiero's?? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Ozzy||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||05-29-2000||03:32 PM||||I'm sure I'll use mine for driving lights whenever I get them.  The previous owner had also installed a switch there, but it was one of those cheapy, generic ones that lit up.  It took a round hole.  I just used a Dremel tool to cut the right size.  This one uses a rectangular hole.  I just figured it might work since it almost looks like it belongs there.  It's not a perfect match in color, but it's awfully close.  And I would assume that it's easily replacable, too.  I'm sure you could get a replacement from Autozone for next to nothing.  On to the next cheap project. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
